From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:20:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] netlink: Increase the receive buffer size

The RTMGRP_LINK socket of netlink_init() uses the default receive
buffer. If many link events wait to be received, the kernel drops the
events that do not fit, and recvfrom() fails with "No buffer space
available". The interface state that the driver wrappers track from
these events then goes out of sync with the kernel.

Request a receive buffer of 256 KiB. The kernel limits the value to
net.core.rmem_max. Keep the default send buffer, since the requests on
this socket are small.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---

--- a/src/drivers/netlink.c
+++ b/src/drivers/netlink.c
@@ -92,6 +92,7 @@ struct netlink_data * netlink_init(struc
 {
 	struct netlink_data *netlink;
 	struct sockaddr_nl local;
+	int rcvbuf = 262144;
 
 	netlink = os_zalloc(sizeof(*netlink));
 	if (netlink == NULL)
@@ -105,6 +106,12 @@ struct netlink_data * netlink_init(struc
 		return NULL;
 	}
 
+	if (setsockopt(netlink->sock, SOL_SOCKET, SO_RCVBUF, &rcvbuf,
+		       sizeof(rcvbuf)) < 0)
+		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG,
+			   "netlink: Failed to set the receive buffer size: %s",
+			   strerror(errno));
+
 	os_memset(&local, 0, sizeof(local));
 	local.nl_family = AF_NETLINK;
 	local.nl_groups = RTMGRP_LINK;
